{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MBBsegdSyLwPpBwmdrW2Uy","type":"tool_result","content":"/* Exact pathwidth (= vertex separation) of trees up to 127 vertices, by the ternary lemma of\n   Ellis, Sudborough & Turner (1994): for a tree S with >= 2 vertices and k >= 1,\n       vs(S) >= k+1  iff  some vertex x has at least three branches (components of S - x) with vs >= k,\n   so vs(S) = max(1, 1 + max_x third_largest{vs(B) : B branch of S at x}).  Memoised over connected\n   vertex subsets (128-bit masks).  Independent of the subset DP and of the pathwidth_solver search;\n   validated against both (see run logs).\n   Input: nauty-gentreeg -p parent arrays, one tree per line (vertices 1..n, parent 0 = root).\n   Usage: treepw [-v] [-p K]   -v: print pw per tree;  -p K: print parent arrays of trees with pw >= K.\n   Always prints a histogram per n to stderr-like final lines \"hist n=.. pw=.. count=..\". */\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\ntypedef unsigned __int128 u128;\n#define MAXN 127\nstatic int n; static u128 adj[MAXN];\nstatic int pc(u128 x){ return __builtin_popcountll((unsigned long long)x) + __builtin_popcountll((unsigned long long)(x>>64)); }\nstatic int lowbit(u128 x){ unsigned long long lo=(unsigned long long)x; if(lo) return __builtin_ctzll(lo); return 64+__builtin_ctzll((unsigned long long)(x>>64)); }\n/* memo: open addressing, generation-stamped */\n#define HBITS 22\n#define HSIZE (1u<<HBITS)\nstatic u128 *hkey; static unsigned char *hval; static unsigned *hgen; static unsigned gen=1; static unsigned long hcount=0;\nstatic unsigned hh(u128 k){ unsigned long long a=(unsigned long long)k, b=(unsigned long long)(k>>64); unsigned long long h=a*0x9E3779B97F4A7C15ULL ^ (b+0x632BE59BD9B4E019ULL)*0xC2B2AE3D27D4EB4FULL; h^=h>>29; return (unsigned)(h>>(64-HBITS)); }\nstatic int memo_get(u128 k){ unsigned i=hh(k); while(hgen[i]==gen){ if(hkey[i]==k) return hval[i]; i=(i+1)&(HSIZE-1);} return -1; }\nstatic void memo_put(u128 k,int v){ unsigned i=hh(k); while(hgen[i]==gen){ i=(i+1)&(HSIZE-1);} hgen[i]=gen; hkey[i]=k; hval[i]=(unsigned char)v; if(++hcount > HSIZE/2){ fprintf(stderr,\"memo full\\n\"); exit(2);} }\nstatic u128 component(u128 R, int y){ u128 comp=(u128)1<<y, fr=comp; while(fr){ u128 nf=0; u128 t=fr; while(t){ int u=lowbit(t); t&=t-1; nf|=adj[u]; } nf&=R; nf&=~comp; comp|=nf; fr=nf; } return comp; }\nstatic int vs(u128 S){\n  int sz=pc(S); if(sz<=1) return 0;\n  int m=memo_get(S); if(m>=0) return m;\n  int best=1; u128 T=S;\n  while(T){ int x=lowbit(T); T&=T-1;\n    u128 R=S&~((u128)1<<x); u128 nb=adj[x]&S; if(pc(nb)<3) continue;\n    /* branches */\n    int vals[MAXN]; int cnt=0; int big=0; u128 rem=nb;\n    u128 comps[MAXN];\n    while(rem){ int y=lowbit(rem); u128 c=component(R,y); rem&=~c; comps[cnt++]=c; if(pc(c)>=2) big++; }\n    if(big<3) continue;\n    for(int i=0;i<cnt;i++) vals[i]= pc(comps[i])>=2 ? vs(comps[i]) : 0;\n    /* third largest */\n    int a=-1,b=-1,c=-1; for(int i=0;i<cnt;i++){ int v=vals[i]; if(v>a){c=b;b=a;a=v;} else if(v>b){c=b;b=v;} else if(v>c){c=v;} }\n    if(c+1>best) best=c+1;\n\"\"\"Helpers: parent arrays (gentreeg -p, 1-indexed, 0 = root) <-> networkx <-> graph6; the C filter\ntreepw and the C solver pathwidth_solver/cli/pathwidth as subprocesses.\"\"\"\nimport subprocess, networkx as nx, itertools, random, sys\nHERE = \"/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/scratch/tree_bound\"\nSOLVER = \"/home/al/dev/MOSP/pathwidth_solver/cli/pathwidth\"\n\ndef parents_to_nx(par):\n    G = nx.Graph(); G.add_nodes_from(range(len(par)))\n    for v, p in enumerate(par):\n        if p > 0: G.add_edge(v, p - 1)\n    return G\n\ndef nx_to_parents(G, root=None):\n    nodes = list(G.nodes()); root = nodes[0] if root is None else root\n    order = list(nx.dfs_preorder_nodes(G, root)); idx = {v: i for i, v in enumerate(order)}\n    par = [0] * len(order)\n    for v in order:\n        if v != root:\n            p = next(iter(nx.dfs_predecessors(G, root).get(v, None),)) if False else None\n    pred = nx.dfs_predecessors(G, root)\n    for v in order:\n        if v != root: par[idx[v]] = idx[pred[v]] + 1\n    return par\n\ndef g6(G):\n    return nx.to_graph6_bytes(nx.convert_node_labels_to_integers(G), header=False).decode().strip()\n\ndef treepw_many(pars):\n    \"\"\"exact pw by the C ternary-lemma filter, list of parent arrays -> list of ints\"\"\"\n    inp = \"\\n\".join(\" \".join(map(str, p)) for p in pars) + \"\\n\"\nreports/scratch/tree_bound/treepw.c\nreports/scratch/tree_bound/treepw_big.c\nreports/scratch/tree_bound/adversarial2.py:4:complete ternary tree (random connected subtrees), at 30..400 vertices.  Exact pw by treepw (n <= 127)\nreports/scratch/tree_bound/adversarial2.py:47:            tp = treepw_many([nx_to_parents(G)])[0] if n <= 127 else None\nreports/scratch/tree_bound/adversarial2.py:49:            if tp is not None and tp != sw: disagree += 1; print(f\"DISAGREE n={n} fam={fam} treepw={tp} solver={sw} ({st}) g6={g6(G)}\", flush=True)\nreports/scratch/tree_bound/adversarial.py:4:'ternary-ish' (each vertex gets 0..3 children).  Exact pw by treepw (n <= 127) and the C solver (all n);\nreports/scratch/tree_bound/adversarial.py:5:every tree with pw >= 3 or with treepw != solver is reported.  Records the max pw per size band.\"\"\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"44e8c6d7-9d93-4ce6-b6cb-7af364193448","uuid":"19442256-2aa4-40b6-a233-ce0ac8b0f8b6","timestamp":"2026-11-01T00:14:27.495Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/* Exact pathwidth (= vertex separation) of trees up to 127 vertices, by the ternary lemma of\n   Ellis, Sudborough & Turner (1994): for a tree S with >= 2 vertices and k >= 1,\n       vs(S) >= k+1  iff  some vertex x has at least three branches (components of S - x) with vs >= k,\n   so vs(S) = max(1, 1 + max_x third_largest{vs(B) : B branch of S at x}).  Memoised over connected\n   vertex subsets (128-bit masks).  Independent of the subset DP and of the pathwid