{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Uzs7unG6MVFhh86KRSW18f","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"node-searching problem on block graphs\" Chou Ko Ho Chen Discrete Applied Mathematics\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"ir.sinica.edu.tw\",\"url\":\"https://ir.sinica.edu.tw/handle/201000000A/39704?&locale=en\"},{\"title\":\"Searching the Nodes of a Graph: Theory and Algorithms\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/0905.3359\"},{\"title\":\"scholars.lib.ntu.edu.tw\",\"url\":\"https://scholars.lib.ntu.edu.tw/bitstreams/a1f03480-b8af-4f43-8612-3a067702458c/download\"},{\"title\":\"Repository logo\",\"url\":\"https://scholars.lib.ntu.edu.tw/entities/publication/0300e99b-f4c5-43a5-a755-2edaffd80ad5\"},{\"title\":\"Graph Searching on Some Subclasses of Chordal Graphs\",\"url\":\"https://ilse.kobv.de/KobvIndexRecord/nat_lic_papers_NLM206915314\"},{\"title\":\"web.iis.sinica.edu.tw\",\"url\":\"https://web.iis.sinica.edu.tw/file/entry/10149/FULLTEXT/zh/tr98015.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"homepage.iis.sinica.edu.tw\",\"url\":\"https://homepage.iis.sinica.edu.tw/file/entry/10158/FULLTEXT/zh/tr97003.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"ir.sinica.edu.tw\",\"url\":\"https://ir.sinica.edu.tw/handle/201000000A/37043\"},{\"title\":\"English  |  正體中文  |  简体中文  |  全文筆數/總筆數 : 83696/83696 (100%)\",\"url\":\"https://ir.lib.ncu.edu.tw/handle/987654321/32313\"},{\"title\":\"Last update: Wed Feb 5 04:57:35 MST 2014\",\"url\":\"https://ftp.math.utah.edu/pub/tex/bib/idx/lncs1997a/1276/0/284-z.html\"}]\n\nThe search turned up the paper itself, plus related work by the same group.\n\n- **The paper:** \"Node-Searching Problem on Block Graphs\" by Hsin-Hung Chou, Ming-Tat Ko, Chin-Wen Ho, and Gen-Huey Chen, published in *Discrete Applied Mathematics* vol. 156 (2008), pp. 55–75. The Sinica repository lists it as Discrete Applied Mathematics 156, with an issue date of 2008.\n- **Main result:** The authors resolve an open question. They adapt the avenue concept, originally proposed for trees, to block graphs, and use it to build an efficient algorithm that computes both search numbers and optimal search strategies. The work answers a question raised by Peng et al. about whether the node-searching problem on block graphs can be solved in polynomial time.\n- **Keywords:** Avenue, block graphs, node-searching, path-width, and vertex separation.\n- **Related thesis:** Chou's 2004 dissertation reports that the node-searching problem on block graphs is polynomial-time solvable. It also covers unicyclic graphs.\n- **Background:** The node-searching problem was introduced by Kirousis and Papadimitriou and is a variant of the graph-searching problem.\n\nI did not retrieve the full text, so I can't confirm the paper's specific algorithmic bounds. The sources above are an institutional repository record, the NTU scholars copy of the PDF, and a thesis abstract.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"44e8c6d7-9d93-4ce6-b6cb-7af364193448","uuid":"f984b96a-c20d-435b-92b4-7b2614119343","timestamp":"2026-11-01T00:16:25.675Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"\"node-searching problem on block graphs\" Chou Ko Ho Chen Discrete Applied Mathematics","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_014EV6vmQ2wxkeSPXRHpybVP","content":[{"title":"ir.sinica.edu.tw","url":"https://ir.sinica.edu.tw/handle/201000000A/39704?&locale=en"},{"title":"Searching the Nodes of a Graph: Theory and Algorithms","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/0905.3359"},{"title":"scholars.lib.ntu.edu.tw","url":"https://scholars.lib.ntu.edu.tw/bitstreams/a1f03480-b8af-4f43-8612-3a067702458c/download"},{"title":"Repository logo","url":"https://scholars.lib.ntu.edu.tw/entities/publication/0300e99b-f4c5-43a5-a755-2edaffd80ad5"},{"title":"Graph Searching on Some Subclasses of Chordal Graphs","url":"https://ilse.kobv.de/KobvIndexRecord/nat_lic_papers_NLM206915314"},{"title":"web.iis.sinica.edu.tw","url":"ht