"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":107,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Item 03 is done and marked `[x]`; the gate passed; nothing further is pending.\n\n**Outcome.** The kill criterion is met: no form `α(ω − 1) + βh + γ` with small integer constants fits the clique trees, so the additive theorem is dropped and item 06 proves the blow-up bound only. The pathwidth of a clique tree is multiplicative in the clique size and the depth: each level of depth costs `(ω − 2)/2` stacks, so the slope in `ω` rises with the depth (3/2, 2, 5/2 at h = 1, 2, 3).\n\n**What was built and measured** (all under `reports/scratch/forest_regime/`, library in `learning/block_trees.py` and `learning/chou_block.py`, 14 new tests):\n- 29 clique trees of the item's grid, all exact in under a minute, plus an 18-cell extension to 936 vertices (11 exact, 7 censored, two of those settled by induced-subgraph monotonicity).\n- 24 caterpillars of cliques, 900 random block trees at n ≤ 120 (898 exact), and the 3,448 incidence-forest instances on record scored for free from their certified optima. Nothing re-solved, `solutions/` untouched, about 4.5 core-hours in all.\n- The C program's values cross-checked against an independent oracle implementing Chou, Ko, Ho and Chen's Theorem 4: 328 of 328 agree on small graphs.\n\n**Findings worth carrying forward.**\n- The literature has the exact answer: node search on block graphs is polynomial, O(c² + bc + n), Discrete Applied Mathematics 156 (2008). Item 06 should cite it rather than prove exactness.\n- A closed form stated after the grid fitted all 29 values and was refuted within the hour by the extension: CT(3,3,3) has a verified width-5 layout where the form said 6. No closed form is conjectured; the description that fits all 33 values with s ≥ 3 is shown to be provably wrong at s = 3 beyond h = 7.\n- Off the structured family the pathwidth is simply the largest pattern: `pw = ω − 1` on 99.8% of the record forests and 92.8% of the random block trees, never more than ω.\n- The additive candidates are not upper bounds; the two multiplicative ones never fail and are loose by a factor of 2 to 5.\n- Two random block trees at n = 120 stayed censored after an hour each at 1.25 × 10¹⁰ nodes; their intervals [6, 7] and [7, 8] stand as intervals.\n\n**Next.** Item 04, the SCOOP instances. Ten items remain, so no `LOOP_COMPLETE` line.","ttft_ms":2267,"type":"result","duration_ms":5524468,"uuid":"776d7a66-8bf5-4549-8e71-2eb2da1316e9","ttft_stream_ms":1609,"time_to_request_ms":339,"first_content_frame_ms":1609,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-fable-5-1":{"inputTokens":2444,"outputTokens":130026,"cacheReadInputTokens":20281494,"cacheCreationInputTokens":300090,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":15.347238500000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":59610,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":300090,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5-1","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":91797,"outputTokens":3041,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":2,"costUSD":0.0307002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1162,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
